<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard wins further trademark suits.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard wins further trademark suits.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co on Wednesday said it has won two trademark infringement suits involving remanufactured printer toner cartridges that are sold as new Hewlett Packard products.</p>
<p>The suits, one in California and another in New York, join what Hewlett-Packard in a statement called &quot;several similar cases over the past year&quot; dealing with remade cartridges.</p>
<p>In California, a U.S. District Court found Supreme Office Products violated a previous court order barring them from selling the cartridges as new products. In New York, a U.S. District Court barred OPG Industries Inc from doing the same.</p>
</text>
